Release Check
    area
    fixture
    try
    expected
    - A01 Sub Examples In A Frame
        area: python
        fixture: Family and Python Probe below
        try: turn on aot.python.enabled, answer Run when asked, then Ctrl+Enter on the family count line of Python Probe
        expected: family count reads 4, since Parent, Child One, Child Two and Other are all rows of the Family frame; in Python the frame has a parent column naming Parent for both children
    - A02 A Parent Reads Its Children
        area: python
        fixture: the total line under Parent in Family
        try: Ctrl+Enter on the total line
        expected: total reads 22, the ages of Child One and Child Two, reached by name from the Example above them
    - A03 A Cell Of A Sub Example
        area: python
        fixture: the youngest line of Python Probe
        try: Ctrl+Enter on it
        expected: youngest reads 10, the age of Child One read through the Family Concept
    - A04 Nested Table Rows Are Rows
        area: python
        fixture: Orchard and the orchard rows line of Python Probe
        try: Ctrl+Enter on orchard rows
        expected: orchard rows reads 6, every row including the indented saplings
    - A05 The Formula Under The Cursor
        area: tables
        fixture: the net cell of row INV-1 in Invoice
        try: put the cursor inside the net derivation of row INV-1, the right-hand one, and press Ctrl+Enter
        expected: only net of INV-1 is computed, 99; vat of INV-1 stays empty
    - A06 A Row Name Runs The Row
        area: tables
        fixture: the name cell of row INV-2 in Invoice
        try: put the cursor on the name INV-2 and press Ctrl+Enter
        expected: both vat and net of INV-2 are computed, 10 and 49
    - A07 One Inlay Per Row
        area: tables
        fixture: the end of row INV-2, after A06
        try: look at the end of row INV-2, and hover the inlay
        expected: one note naming both cells, a tick then vat, net then the time taken; the tooltip has one line per cell
    - A08 Hover Per Cell
        area: tables
        fixture: the values of row INV-2, after A06
        try: hover the value 10 and then the value 49 on row INV-2
        expected: each hover names the derivation of its own cell, price times 0.2 for vat and price minus 1 for net
    - A09 A Pipe Inside A Cell
        area: tables
        fixture: the Pipe Probe table
        try: Ctrl+Enter on row P1
        expected: length reads 3; the pipe inside the string never split the cell, so the row has three cells, no error
    - A10 A Calculated Column
        area: tables
        fixture: the vat column of Invoice
        try: put the cursor on any vat cell, press Ctrl+dot and choose Define vat for the whole column, then Ctrl+Enter on the Invoice header
        expected: the header becomes vat followed by a double equals and price times 0.2; each vat cell keeps only its value, and the run fills the empty ones
    - A11 Own Derivation Beats The Header
        area: tables
        fixture: the Squad table
        try: Ctrl+Enter on the Squad header
        expected: Blue and Green fill with 4 from the header; Red keeps 5 from its own derivation, with a warning that 5 is not 4
    - A12 A Bare Line Writes Concepts
        area: python
        fixture: the first bare derivation line near the end of this file
        try: Ctrl+Enter on that line
        expected: a Courier Run table appears directly under it at the top level with rows 1 and 2; the Depot table above the line is filled where it stands with Durban; the inlay says 2 Concepts
    - A13 A Concept With Its Own Derivation
        area: python
        fixture: the second bare derivation line, and Fleet
        try: Ctrl+Enter on the second bare line
        expected: a Spare Part table appears under it; Fleet is left to its own derivation, and the line says so in red
    - A14 Reading What A Bare Line Wrote
        area: python
        fixture: Courier Probe, after A12
        try: Ctrl+Enter on the stops line
        expected: stops reads 2, read live from the table the bare line returned
    - A15 Nothing Is Deleted
        area: python
        fixture: the first bare derivation line, after A12
        try: delete the Depot entry from its dictionary and press Ctrl+Enter on it again
        expected: Depot stays in the file; the inlay ends with Depot no longer written
    - A16 A Bare Line Parks
        area: parking
        fixture: the whole file, after A12
        try: Ctrl+Shift+backtick, look, then Ctrl+Shift+backtick again
        expected: both bare lines leave the file whole and the tables they wrote stay; aot.files gets release 1.12.formulas; the second press puts each bare line back above the table that stood beneath it
    - A17 No Flip Lightbulb
        area: editor
        fixture: Bicycle
        try: put the cursor anywhere in Bicycle and press Ctrl+dot; then press Ctrl+K T twice
        expected: the lightbulb offers no flip; Ctrl+K T writes Bicycle as a table and the second press writes it back as lines
    - A18 Column Keys On A Declaration
        area: editor
        fixture: the colour line directly under Bicycle
        try: put the cursor on that colour line and press Alt+Shift+Left; then Ctrl+Z
        expected: colour goes from the declaration and from both Examples in one edit; Tab on a declaration line still indents
    - A19 The Name Column Is Safe
        area: editor
        fixture: the Kite table
        try: put the cursor on K1 and press Alt+Shift+Left, then Alt+Right, then Ctrl+Alt+Right
        expected: nothing changes, and the status bar says the first column names the Concept and its Examples
    - A20 A Part Is Not Its Whole
        area: linter
        fixture: the first nine lines of release 1.12 errors.aot
        try: open it
        expected: red squiggles on the inner Parent, on the lowercase root row under Mid, and on the nested Top row of Nested Probe, each pointing at its parent
    - A21 A Lone Equals And A Loose Bound
        area: linter
        fixture: the last two lines of release 1.12 errors.aot
        try: look at its last two lines
        expected: an error that the equals sign stands alone, and an error that the bound has no attribute
    - A22 A Maintained Note
        area: repository
        fixture: Lantern here and Lantern in release 1.12 peer.aot
        try: save this file
        expected: a line under Lantern appears saying 2 more in release 1.12 peer.aot, Ctrl+clickable
    - A23 A Stale Note Goes
        area: repository
        fixture: after A22
        try: rename Lantern to Torch in release 1.12 peer.aot and save it, then save this file
        expected: the 2 more line under Lantern here is deleted; with aot.autoReconcile off it stays and warns that it is stale instead
    - A24 Hover Shows Content
        area: godel
        fixture: Instrument
        try: hover the names Flute and Cello
        expected: a Content section with G as a factorisation; Cello shows section strings from Instrument with its line; Flute shows section woodwind as its own and an override of strings; each names its nearest sibling and how it differs
    - A25 A Value Every Child States
        area: godel
        fixture: Boat
        try: look at the yellow squiggle on Boat, press Ctrl+dot, choose Move hull wood up to Boat
        expected: hull wood is written once under Boat and taken off Canoe and Kayak; the warning goes
    - A26 A Column Every Row States
        area: godel
        fixture: the Receipt table
        try: Ctrl+dot on the Receipt warning, Move currency ZAR up to Receipt
        expected: the currency column is dropped, and Receipt gets a line of its own holding currency ZAR with the table filed beneath it
    - A27 A Default Nothing Keeps
        area: godel
        fixture: Meal
        try: Ctrl+dot on the warning on course main, Keep just course
        expected: the line becomes course alone; the warning goes
    - A28 One Content Two Names
        area: godel
        fixture: Toaster here and Grill in release 1.12 peer.aot
        try: open both files
        expected: each warns that the two carry exactly the same attributes and values, linking the other; Ctrl+dot offers to rename or to keep them apart
    - A29 Stable Numbers
        area: godel
        fixture: aot.files godel.tsv
        try: save this file, then run node verify.js on this file with the godel flag for Flute twice, adding an attribute to Boat between the runs
        expected: aot.files gets godel.tsv; the primes for Flute are the same before and after the new attribute
    - A30 A Diff That Sees Renames
        area: godel
        fixture: this file in git
        try: commit this file, rename Kayak to Sea Kayak, then run node verify.js with the diff-rev flag, HEAD and this file
        expected: one finding, renamed, with no removed or added lines for anything under it
    - A31 Merge By Meaning
        area: git
        fixture: the walkthrough in docs features-1.12
        try: run AOT Set Up Git Merge for aot Files, then follow the walkthrough in a scratch repository
        expected: the rename and the value change merge cleanly, and the value changed two ways conflicts on that one line
    - A32 Python In WSL
        area: wsl
        fixture: this file, opened from WSL with Remote WSL
        try: install the extension in WSL, enable Python, Ctrl+Enter on Python Probe; then AOT Set Up Python Environment
        expected: python3 runs with no python on PATH; the environment goes to aot.files .venv-linux and the Windows .venv is left alone; Show Python Environment says memory is a data-size limit
